+# Changelog
+
+## 2026-10-30 - Add an endpoint GET /api/v1/links that lists the most recent
+
+Added `GET /api/v1/links`, which returns the most recently created short links as a bare JSON array ordered newest first by creation time (ties broken by id, descending). The optional `limit` query parameter defaults to 20 and accepts 1 to 100. Out-of-range, empty or non-integer values return HTTP 400 with an `application/problem+json` body through the existing error handling. Each item has exactly the same JSON shape as `GET /api/v1/links/{code}`. The list is unauthenticated, like that endpoint, applies no per-caller filtering, and includes deactivated and expired links, because those are still retrievable by code. Results are fetched with a database-bounded query. There is no pagination or total count, and existing endpoints, error handling, schema and tests are unchanged.
